WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.260
Before the review, two versions arrive on
the desk.

2
00:00:04.060 --> 00:00:05.080
The title is familiar.

3
00:00:05.740 --> 00:00:06.940
The revision is different.

4
00:00:07.320 --> 00:00:10.940
Which document governs the work, and are
the references behind it

5
00:00:10.940 --> 00:00:14.640
actually present? The reviewer needs more
than a search result.

6
00:00:15.220 --> 00:00:18.840
They need a route back to the wording, its
context and its history.

7
00:00:19.540 --> 00:00:23.060
This is the problem Cortessa is being built
around:

8
00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:27.220
controlled documents, questions that can be
traced, and people who

9
00:00:27.220 --> 00:00:28.860
remain accountable for the decision.

10
00:00:28.860 --> 00:00:33.540
We will follow that route through the
actual product, using public NASA

11
00:00:33.540 --> 00:00:35.040
documents as a demonstration.

12
00:00:35.980 --> 00:00:38.040
The people and workplaces are illustrative.

13
00:00:38.680 --> 00:00:39.560
Start with Audit.

14
00:00:40.120 --> 00:00:43.520
It cross-references the selected corpus and
surfaces documentary

15
00:00:43.520 --> 00:00:45.160
questions for human review:

16
00:00:45.760 --> 00:00:50.360
a superseded revision, an uncertain
reference, or a cited document that

17
00:00:50.360 --> 00:00:51.280
is not held.

18
00:00:51.920 --> 00:00:56.320
On the graph, a document on one side points
to the references it cites.

19
00:00:56.320 --> 00:00:59.720
Follow one relationship into the candidate
behind it.

20
00:01:00.020 --> 00:01:03.860
In this public example, a held document
cites a reference that the

21
00:01:03.860 --> 00:01:05.240
corpus does not hold.

22
00:01:05.800 --> 00:01:09.800
The candidate identifies the citing source
and passage, so the next step

23
00:01:09.800 --> 00:01:13.780
is inspectable. The important result is not
the colour of a warning.

24
00:01:14.320 --> 00:01:15.560
It is the evidence route:

25
00:01:15.920 --> 00:01:20.040
which document made the reference, where it
appears, and what the held

26
00:01:20.040 --> 00:01:24.480
corpus contains. A missing document becomes
a visible review question.

27
00:01:24.480 --> 00:01:28.200
That gap remains part of the evidence the
reviewer examines.

28
00:01:28.760 --> 00:01:31.460
The reviewer can now decide what to inspect
next.

29
00:01:32.140 --> 00:01:33.240
Open the cited passage.

30
00:01:33.660 --> 00:01:35.400
Then open the original document.

31
00:01:35.820 --> 00:01:39.080
The source matters because a sentence can
change meaning when it is

32
00:01:39.080 --> 00:01:43.020
separated from its surrounding wording,
revision or applicability.

33
00:01:43.560 --> 00:01:46.900
A matching phrase alone does not settle the
engineering question.

34
00:01:47.480 --> 00:01:51.640
Here, the reviewer follows the reference
back to the page and examines

35
00:01:51.640 --> 00:01:56.020
that context. They can compare the relevant
revision and check whether

36
00:01:56.020 --> 00:01:58.400
the wording governs this particular review.

37
00:01:59.240 --> 00:02:01.160
Cortessa keeps that route inspectable.

38
00:02:01.660 --> 00:02:03.220
It surfaces a cited candidate;

39
00:02:03.760 --> 00:02:06.960
the responsible specialist examines the
evidence and decides what

40
00:02:06.960 --> 00:02:09.340
follows. That is the working relationship:

41
00:02:09.760 --> 00:02:13.080
the product brings the documentary issue
into view, and the human

42
00:02:13.080 --> 00:02:14.940
challenges it against the source.

43
00:02:15.460 --> 00:02:18.980
The same discipline applies when the
reviewer has a specific question.

44
00:02:18.980 --> 00:02:23.440
In Ask, open the citation and inspect the
source behind the response.

45
00:02:24.140 --> 00:02:27.060
This recorded public example is labelled
Draft.

46
00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:31.300
A citation is available to inspect, while
the response remains

47
00:02:31.300 --> 00:02:34.380
explicitly Draft, not a verified
conclusion.

48
00:02:34.880 --> 00:02:37.260
Another recorded example is marked Refused.

49
00:02:37.920 --> 00:02:41.180
The product can decline to give an answer
that the evidence does not

50
00:02:41.180 --> 00:02:45.620
support. Verified, Draft and Refused have
different meanings.

51
00:02:45.620 --> 00:02:48.160
Verified establishes provenance:

52
00:02:48.500 --> 00:02:50.340
wording is anchored to a source.

53
00:02:50.900 --> 00:02:54.560
It does not establish correctness,
applicability or approval.

54
00:02:55.220 --> 00:02:58.780
The reviewer still decides whether the
passage answers the question and

55
00:02:58.780 --> 00:03:00.040
whether it governs the work.

56
00:03:00.320 --> 00:03:04.080
They have a source to inspect and a
question to resolve, rather than an

57
00:03:04.080 --> 00:03:06.080
unexplained instruction to accept.

58
00:03:06.580 --> 00:03:11.240
At a wind farm, a nuclear facility or a
carrier deck, the scenery

59
00:03:11.240 --> 00:03:13.800
changes; the evidence question remains.

60
00:03:13.800 --> 00:03:18.280
In aviation planning, it may concern the
documentary basis for the next

61
00:03:18.280 --> 00:03:19.400
human approval step.

62
00:03:19.740 --> 00:03:23.100
Before a police briefing, it may be a
question about superseded

63
00:03:23.100 --> 00:03:28.080
guidance. These are illustrative
situations, not customer deployments.

64
00:03:28.800 --> 00:03:31.220
The documentary task is the link between
them.

65
00:03:31.460 --> 00:03:34.200
The authorised professional records the
judgement through their

66
00:03:34.200 --> 00:03:38.660
organisation's process. Cortessa surfaces
evidence for that review.

67
00:03:39.060 --> 00:03:42.180
Human authority stays with the people
responsible for the work.

68
00:03:42.180 --> 00:03:44.800
That evidence work begins locally.

69
00:03:45.420 --> 00:03:49.640
Each Cortessa engineer box holds its
documents, ingestion pipeline,

70
00:03:49.860 --> 00:03:51.240
index and resident model.

71
00:03:51.800 --> 00:03:55.600
The on-device model is the standard
generated experience, without a

72
00:03:55.600 --> 00:03:58.920
public-cloud dependency. Analysis stays on-
box.

73
00:03:59.440 --> 00:04:02.820
If the selected model is unavailable, that
state is made explicit.

74
00:04:03.660 --> 00:04:07.400
Separate source extracts are not relabelled
as a successful generated

75
00:04:07.400 --> 00:04:10.980
answer. This keeps the working context
close to the reviewer.

76
00:04:10.980 --> 00:04:14.620
It also keeps the organisation's access
rules and approval

77
00:04:14.620 --> 00:04:16.300
responsibilities in the story.

78
00:04:16.960 --> 00:04:19.940
Sovereignty is a working boundary around
the evidence and its use.

79
00:04:20.400 --> 00:04:22.360
The local product supports that boundary;

80
00:04:22.800 --> 00:04:25.560
a label on an answer does not replace human
judgement.

81
00:04:26.280 --> 00:04:30.300
The wider design connects those local boxes
through departmental nodes

82
00:04:30.300 --> 00:04:34.240
to an on-site hub, entirely inside the site
boundary.

83
00:04:34.800 --> 00:04:39.040
What is intended to travel is an explicitly
approved, signed revision,

84
00:04:39.460 --> 00:04:41.580
carrying its lineage and permitted scope.

85
00:04:42.160 --> 00:04:44.440
A receiving reviewer still examines it.

86
00:04:44.940 --> 00:04:48.760
Arrival does not make it the governing
source or automatically add it to

87
00:04:48.760 --> 00:04:50.020
another searchable corpus.

88
00:04:50.780 --> 00:04:54.580
The self-sufficient local product and
governed exchange foundations

89
00:04:54.580 --> 00:04:59.180
exist. Authenticated peer transport,
provisioning and production rollout

90
00:04:59.180 --> 00:05:00.400
remain in development.

91
00:05:01.160 --> 00:05:03.140
That distinction stays visible here:

92
00:05:03.620 --> 00:05:07.760
solid local foundations, a developing site
network, and human approval

93
00:05:07.760 --> 00:05:09.800
at the points where authority changes.

94
00:05:10.540 --> 00:05:14.800
The aim is a document thread people can
inspect, with scope and history

95
00:05:14.800 --> 00:05:16.840
preserved across the organisation.

96
00:05:17.300 --> 00:05:21.480
Begin with one bounded document workflow
and a corpus cleared for the

97
00:05:21.480 --> 00:05:25.900
evaluation. Name the reviewers and agree
what evidence they need before

98
00:05:25.900 --> 00:05:26.940
the test starts.

99
00:05:27.460 --> 00:05:29.020
Include the awkward cases:

100
00:05:29.460 --> 00:05:33.600
uncertain revisions, missing references,
difficult source material and

101
00:05:33.600 --> 00:05:35.460
questions whose answers are absent.

102
00:05:35.460 --> 00:05:39.920
Watch how people find the source, challenge
a candidate and record their

103
00:05:39.920 --> 00:05:44.240
judgement. Then decide what Cortessa has
demonstrated in your own review

104
00:05:44.240 --> 00:05:46.680
process, and what needs further work.

105
00:05:47.180 --> 00:05:49.880
See Audit and Ask against evidence you can
inspect.

106
00:05:50.400 --> 00:05:54.300
Get in touch to arrange a Cortessa
demonstration and discuss a scoped

107
00:05:54.300 --> 00:05:57.680
evaluation. Cortessa. Sovereign document
intelligence.
